# generated build output (audius demo) — recipe in examples/audius/audius-build/RUNBOOK.md
# Leading **/ on purpose: an anchored `audius-build/…` silently stopped matching
# when these moved under examples/, which un-ignored every artifact below.
**/audius-build/audius_cache.json
**/audius-build/edges_all.json
**/audius-build/cdn/
**/audius-build/stage/
**/audius-build/*.log
**/.wrangler/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/dist/**

# ── audius-large-build ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ~37 GB of build artifacts. The SCRIPTS here are tracked on purpose — dump_source.py,
# embed_stage.py, bootstrap.py, repair_vocab_edges.py, restore.sh, fetch-dump.sh and
# RUNBOOK.md are the whole reproducible pipeline. Everything they PRODUCE is ignored:
# rebuilding from the dump is a documented recipe, and none of it belongs in history.
#
# The dump is a PRODUCTION social database — it contains chat_message and
# chat_blocked_users. Never commit it, and delete it once extraction is done.
**/audius-large-build/dump.bin
**/audius-large-build/*.bin
**/audius-large-build/*.jsonl
# 4.9 GB of baked shards (audius-large + audius-home) and the codebook.
**/audius-large-build/cdn/
# 6.9 GB: the staged volume_*.json graph and the 2.4 GB edges.sqlite. This is the one
# that would actually have been pushed — 17 files, none of them small.
**/audius-large-build/stage/
# Postgres data if restore.sh is ever pointed at a bind mount instead of a volume.
**/audius-large-build/pgdata/
# Build logs, up to ~7 MB each.
**/audius-large-build/*.log

# ── belt and braces ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each app carries its own .gitignore for `dist` and `public/cdn`, which is where the
# staged snapshot lands (78 MB for audius-demo alone). Repeat them here so a new app
# copied from an existing one cannot leak a snapshot before someone notices its
# .gitignore did not come along.
**/public/cdn/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.ndjson.gz

# Local env. Machine-specific (ports, tunnel URLs), and the convention every vite app
# here follows. `.env.local.example` is committed instead, so the wiring is
# discoverable without pinning anyone to this machine's ports.
.env.local
.env.*.local
